/// Isolates run work in parallel, each on its own thread with its own
/// memory. `isolate.run(f)` runs `f` on a new isolate and gives a future of
/// its result; `isolate.spawn(f)` starts one that runs until `f` is done.
/// Values they use are copied, and channels carry messages between them.

/// Returns how many processor cores the machine has.
pub extern fn cores() -> int as "vx_cores"
